@id lane_carter
# DRAFT
# The carter passing through the lane with his wagon at dusk, nights 1 to 6: a line a night.
# His own flags: lane_carter_<night> (talked to him tonight).
== start
-> start_known [if talked_n0_carter]
-> start_new

== start_known
(The carter, walking at his horse's head, his wagon empty.)
Carter {calm}: Porter. They kept you, then.
-> tonight

== start_new
(A carter walking at his horse's head, his wagon empty.)
-> tonight

== again
-> back [if night=1] [if lane_carter_1]
-> back [if night=2] [if lane_carter_2]
-> back [if night=3] [if lane_carter_3]
-> back [if night=4] [if lane_carter_4]
-> back [if night=5] [if lane_carter_5]
-> back [if night=6] [if lane_carter_6]
-> hello

== hello
(The carter, walking at his horse's head.)
-> tonight

== back
Carter {weary}: I've said my piece, porter.
-> end

== tonight
-> n1 [if night=1]
-> n2 [if night=2]
-> n3 [if night=3]
-> n4 [if night=4]
-> n5 [if night=5]
-> n6 [if night=6]

# Night 1
== n1 [set lane_carter_1]
Carter {amused}: You've the look of it already. Pale. They'll have you white as a tallow candle by Advent.
-> n1_ask

== n1_ask
* Where are you bound? -> n1_bound

== n1_bound
Carter {wary, glance}: Out through Aldgate before they shut it. I don't sleep inside these walls. Not any more.
-> end

# Night 2
== n2 [set lane_carter_2]
-> n2_pond [if died_merchant]
-> n2_rain

== n2_pond
Carter {sad}: That merchant of yours. I passed him on the road yesterday, singing. A voice like a bull.
-> n2_ask

== n2_rain
Carter {weary}: Roads are soup from here to Mile End.
-> n2_ask

== n2_ask
* Go carefully. -> n2_care

== n2_care
Carter {amused}: Always do. That's why I'm still carting.
-> end

# Night 3
== n3 [set lane_carter_3]
-> n3_jankin [if died_jankin]
-> n3_road

== n3_jankin
Carter {sad}: Jankin. I carted his barrels, once, when he made barrels. Before his wife went.
-> n3_road

== n3_road
Carter {grave}: No pilgrims on the road today. Not one. Word's getting about.
-> n3_ask

== n3_ask
* Word of what? -> n3_word

== n3_word
Carter {wary}: Of your abbey, porter. What else is there?
-> end

# Night 4
== n4 [set lane_carter_4]
Carter {afraid}: Fog on the road, thick as fleece. I near put the wagon in the ditch by the white chapel.
(He crosses himself.)
Carter {grave}: There's been enough in that ditch.
-> n4_ask

== n4_ask
* God keep you on the road. -> n4_bless

== n4_bless
Carter {grave}: Keep your blessings for them inside, porter. They need them more.
-> end

# Night 5
== n5 [set lane_carter_5]
Carter {afraid}: I'm not stopping tonight. Last load, then I'm out of the gate, and I'll not be back till it's over.
-> n5_ask

== n5_ask
* Till what's over? -> n5_over

== n5_over
Carter {afraid, look away}: Whatever this is.
-> end

# Night 6
== n6 [set lane_carter_6]
Carter {weary}: Snow. I'll be lucky to get the wagon through Aldgate in this.
(He looks at your face a long moment.)
Carter {pleading}: There's room on the back, porter. Same as there was coming in.
-> n6_ask

== n6_ask
* I can't. -> n6_no
* (Shake your head.) -> n6_no

== n6_no
Carter {sad, nod}: No. I didn't think so.
-> end

== leave
Carter {grave}: Mind yourself, porter.
